{
  "spdx": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
  "description": "Expectations the vendored hoshidicts engine does not meet today, recorded per corpus row. YomitanCorpusTest (T1) validates the corpus itself; YomitanEngineConformanceTest (T2) re-derives every verdict and fails both on an unlisted failure and on a listed row that starts passing, so this file can never hide a regression and never goes stale silently.",
  "entryFormat": "corpus: corpus file name; index: 0-based line index in that file; subject: the row's identity field (transforms: source, normalization: op); detail: the row's expected value (transforms: term, normalization: input); gap: key into gaps.",
  "yomitan": {
    "commit": "e7334a96106a6c74e6fa75bd33a5ea1219d92712",
    "commitShort": "e7334a9"
  },
  "gaps": {
    "historical-kana-forms-unsupported": "The engine's deinflection rules carry only modern kana forms; Yomitan also lists 歴史的仮名遣い source variants (は行→わ行, ひ→い, ふ→う, ゐ→い, and やう/ませう/さう/からう + う), so these rows have no candidate in the engine.",
    "missing-transform-group:-やしない": "Yomitan has a `-やしない` transform (やしない/やしません/やしない+た → る); the vendored `Deinflector::init_transforms` has no such group.",
    "missing-transform-group:-ふ": "Yomitan has a `-ふ` transform (ふ→う, and う/よう volitional); the vendored `Deinflector::init_transforms` has no such group.",
    "single-character-input-identity-only": "`Deinflector::deinflect` returns only the identity candidate when the input is shorter than two code points (`if (text_len > 1) … else result.emplace_back(text, NONE, trace)`), so a single-character source (し, 来, 來, き) can never reach its dictionary form.",
    "katakana-to-hiragana-keep-prolonged-sound-marks-unsupported": "`katakana_to_hiragana` in the engine's `text_processor.cpp` always rewrites the prolonged sound mark to the preceding vowel; the engine exposes no `keepProlongedSoundMarks` mode."
  },
